134:Provenance is the inspectable source lineage of a claim, including where the evidence came from and why it was trusted.
143:Source Conflict Trigger occurs when retrieved sources materially disagree and the disagreement could change the answer or recommendation.
146:Citation-grounded synthesis is synthesis that remains tied to actual retrieved evidence rather than conclusion-first paraphrasing.
149:Agentic RAG is a retrieval mode in which a reasoning layer actively evaluates source quality, resolves contradictions, decomposes complex evidence needs, and may invoke additional retrieval or external tools when justified.
152:An Evidence Pack is the minimized set of retrieved material passed into answer generation or downstream processing.
155:Composite evidence is support assembled from multiple distinct fragments or sources because no single source sufficiently covers the claim.
158:Currentness is the justified confidence that a retrieved source reflects the relevant present state rather than historical or stale context.
